<%# locals: bottle, (optional) tone (:dark default, :light), (optional) size (:md default, :sm)
    The one way a bottle's photo is shown anywhere: identity bands and list rows.

    PORTRAIT, not square: a bottle is tall, and a square crop of a phone
    snapshot spends most of the frame on the counter behind it.

    No backing plate. On the dark bands the old cream plate read as a sticker
    stuck on top, and per the design system's de-carding rule it was a second
    elevated surface. The tile sits on the surface behind a hairline ring
    instead, and the drawn placeholder occupies the same footprint so two
    bottles side by side always agree.

    tone: matches the ground it sits on. size: :md for identity bands, :sm for
    list rows, where it should fill the row rather than float in it. Both keep
    the same 4:5 portrait. %>
<%
  dark = local_assigns.fetch(:tone, :dark) == :dark
  small = local_assigns.fetch(:size, :md) == :sm
  # Literal class strings — Tailwind can't see interpolated fragments.
  box = small ? "h-16 w-12" : "h-20 w-16"
  skin = dark ? "bg-oak ring-cream/15" : "bg-whiskey-50 ring-gray-200"
%>
<div class="shrink-0 overflow-hidden rounded-xl ring-1 <%= skin %>">
  <% if bottle.display_image %>
    <%= image_tag bottle.display_image.variant(:portrait),
        class: "#{box} object-cover", alt: bottle.name %>
  <% else %>
    <div class="flex <%= box %> items-center justify-center">
      <%= render "bottles/placeholder", bottle: bottle,
          size: (small ? "h-12" : "h-14"), tone: (dark ? :dark : :light) %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
